<title>USA: CyberGuard Q3 revenues increase.</title>
<headline>CyberGuard Q3 revenues increase.</headline>
<dateline>FT. LAUDERDALE, Fla. 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>CyberGuard Corp said Thursday its revenues in the fiscal third quarter ended March 31 rose to $4.1 million from $2.5 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>The company attributed the rise to increased awareness and indirect distribution of its products and its recent E3 government certification in the United Kingdom under the European Information Technology Security Evaluation Criteria.</p>
<p>The company said it plans to complement its family of products with encryption and authentication products, systems and services from TradeWave, its newly-acquired subsidiary.</p>
<p>CyberGuard provides intranet and Internet security solutions.</p>
</text>
